  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "COLUMNS returns 1 for non-empty scalars, #REF! for multi-area references, and #VALUE! for blank or omitted arguments",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, COLUMNS(array) returns the column count of a single-area reference (COLUMNS(A1:C5) -> 3, COLUMNS(INDEX(A1:C3,2,0)) -> 3) or array constant (COLUMNS({1,2,3}) -> 3, COLUMNS({1;2;3}) -> 1), returns 1 for a scalar number, text, or logical (COLUMNS(5) -> 1), propagates an error argument (COLUMNS(#N/A) -> #N/A), returns #REF! for a multi-area reference (COLUMNS((A1:A3,B1:B2)) -> #REF!), and returns #VALUE! for a blank/omitted argument (COLUMNS(CHOOSE(2,1,)) -> #VALUE!). All 3,350 full-bank COLUMNS rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in DnaCalc cfunc_m3_6 (reference_result and lookup_edges) and jnt_lookup rows 50-56 (Excel 16.0.20527.20088); 3,350/3,350 full-bank rows match.",
